<title>AUSTRALIA: Singapore Airlines dwarfs new partners.</title>
<headline>Singapore Airlines dwarfs new partners.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Singapore Airlines, Air New Zealand and Australian airline Ansett issued the following data on their businesses after forging an alliance on Friday.</p>
<p>The figures are for the airlines' 1995/96 years. The Ansett data group together Ansett Australia and Ansett International.</p>
<p>		    Singapore	Ansett	   Air New Zealand</p>
<p>		    Airlines</p>
<p>Total revenue   US$4.83 bln    US$2.47 bln    US$2.07 bln</p>
<p>Passengers</p>
<p>carried	   11.06 million	12.16 million	6.6 million</p>
<p>Revenue</p>
<p>passenger kms   50.05 million	15.47 million	20.1 million</p>
<p>Employees	 27, 241	  17,977	   9,929</p>
<p>Countries</p>
<p>served*	   43		 8		  19</p>
<p>Daily</p>
<p>departures	181		380		520</p>
<p>Operating fleet 80		 71**	     72**</p>
<p>* over 200 destinations are served by the carriers' international and domestic operations</p>
<p>** including aircraft operating domestically</p>
<p>-- Melbourne bureau 613-9286-1421</p>
</text>
